2. PERMISSIONS — WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

   Subject to Sections 3 and 4, you are granted the following rights
   free of charge:

   a) VIEW — You may read and study the Software's source code.

   b) USE — You may run the Software for any purpose, including
      commercial purposes, as an individual or on behalf of any
      organization of any size, on any number of devices.

   c) INTERNAL MODIFICATION — You may modify the Software for your own
      use or for Your Organization's internal use (for example to
      support a corporate proxy, certificate store, or internal
      infrastructure). A Modified Version may not be Publicly
      Distributed (Section 3a), and Section 3(d) still applies.

   d) INTERNAL SHARING — You may copy the Software, including a
      Modified Version made under Section 2(c), and deploy or share it
      within Your Organization and with the contractors working for it,
      provided that no Public Distribution occurs.

   e) EXTENSIONS — You and others may create, publish, and sell
      Extensions under terms of your own choosing. An Extension is an
      independent work and is not a Modified Version. Section 3(c)
      applies to how an Extension refers to the Author and the
      Software.

   f) YOUR OUTPUT — As between you and the Author, Your Output belongs
      to you. You may use it for any purpose, including commercially.
      Terms of the AI model or service that generated it may also
      apply.

   g) CONTRIBUTING — You may create a copy of the Software on a public
      code-hosting platform solely to prepare a contribution to the
      Author's official repository, provided that the copy is not
      otherwise used, promoted, or distributed.

