3. RESTRICTIONS — WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT PERMISSION

   The following require explicit prior written permission from the
   Author:

   a) PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION — Except as allowed in Section 2(g), you may
      not publish, release, distribute, mirror, or host the Software or
      a Modified Version for anyone outside Your Organization,
      including on platforms such as GitHub, GitLab, package indexes,
      container registries, app stores, or any other repository or
      website.

   b) SELLING AND SERVICES — You may not sell, license, sublicense,
      rent, or host the Software or a Modified Version as a product or
      service for others, or include it in a product or service offered
      to others. Using the Software to do your own work, including paid
      work for clients, is not restricted by this clause.

   c) REBRANDING AND NAMES — You may not remove or alter copyright
      notices, credits, or this license file, and may not present the
      Software as your own original work. You may not use the names
      "Nukerhugo" or "Nukerhugo CLI", or the Author's logos, for a
      Modified Version, or in a way that suggests that an Extension or
      other product is made, endorsed, or certified by the Author.
      Factual statements such as "works with Nukerhugo CLI" are
      allowed.

   d) CIRCUMVENTION — You may not modify or use the Software to
      circumvent, evade, or interfere with the usage limits,
      authentication, billing, or access controls of the Nukerhugo
      Services, for example by creating accounts or keys to avoid
      limits.

